  "methods": "MethodsEligibility criteriaPICO: Population adults with type 2 diabetes · Intervention / exposure metformin · Comparator no metformin · Outcomes CRC incidenceStudy types: any design (no restriction)No limit on the publication yearAn abstract of at least 150 characters is requiredSearched with English queries; no language filter was appliedInclusion criteria (the planner's): Adults with type 2 diabetesExclusion criteria (the planner's): EditorialsInformation sources and searchSearched on 5 October 2026Review completed on 5 October 2026Records per source (before de-duplication): PubMed 30 · Europe PMC 12 · Europe PMC (RCT search) 4 · OpenAlex 9Records identified before de-duplication 55Search queries (2)1metformin colorectal cancer2metformin CRC cohortScreening and selectionRecords with an abstract were ranked by relevance to the question, and at most 60 top records were screenedTitle and abstract screening by deepseek/deepseek-v4-proBorderline records (relevance 35–70) were scored again by the same model (not an independent vote)Included records scoring below 35 were not analysed, unless the two votes disagreed or fewer than 3 would remainNarrative reviews were left out when at least 3 primary studies or systematic reviews were availableAt most 30 records were analysed, in order of relevanceData extraction and verificationOnly titles and abstracts were read, never the full textData were extracted twice by the same model (deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro)Every number had to be found in the abstract (its quoted sentence matching at least 90%); a number that failed is left blank, never guessedVerified 6 of 7 numbers (86%)Risk of bias assessmentA model judged each study's risk of bias from its abstract as Low / Some concerns / High / UnclearCriteria: study design, sample size, control of confounding, and completeness of reportingNo full standard tool (such as RoB 2 or ROBINS) was usedSynthesisEach study's result was tabled by outcome, then the points where studies agree and conflict were found; SR/MAs are not counted again with the primary studies they may includeSynthesis by deepseek/deepseek-v4-proCertainty of evidenceGRADE-lite: a baseline from study design, risk of bias, consistency and precision, which the model may move by at most one level with a reason; not an expert GRADE assessmentModels and versionsModels: Screening, extraction, second extraction, synthesis deepseek/deepseek-v4-proModel preset budgetRun time 58 sAutomationEvery step was done automatically by language models; no human reviewer screened, extracted or checked. Only abstracts were read, so data reported only in the full text can be missed.Automated rapid systematic review from abstracts only; not medical advice.",
